gridforge source package
========================

Built by tools/deb/make-deb.sh from the GridForge repository; this debian/
directory lives in the repository as packaging/debian/ and is copied in.

Component tarballs (dpkg-source 3.0 (quilt), several upstream tarballs):

  gridforge_<v>.orig.tar.xz           GridForge, git archive of the release
  gridforge_<v>.orig-netgen.tar.xz    our Netgen fork at the submodule's
                                      commit (netgen/COMMIT), with its
                                      version.txt, as Netgen reads it
                                      without git
  gridforge_<v>.orig-ccx.tar.bz2      ccx_2.23.src.tar.bz2, unchanged
  gridforge_<v>.orig-spooles.tar.gz   spooles.2.2.tgz, unchanged

The ccx and SPOOLES tarballs are pinned by SHA-256 in tools/build-ccx.sh.
Carrying them here makes this source package hold the source of the ccx
gridforge-calculix ships (GPL-2).

For now, not yet "the Debian way" (David, 2026-11-18)
-----------------------------------------------------

Debian generally wants a package to use the archive's libraries, not
copies of its own. Two parts are carried here because the archive does
not yet have them in the versions GridForge is tested with:

* Netgen. GridForge uses Netgen past 6.2.2608; Ubuntu 26.04 has 6.2.2601.
  When Debian's libnglib reaches GridForge's pinned commit (or GridForge's
  fork carries nothing of its own on top of a released Netgen), gridforge
  should depend on libnglib-dev/libnglib and drop the netgen component and
  /usr/lib/gridforge/libnglib.so, libngcore.so.

* ccx. GridForge ships CalculiX 2.23, the version its tests and examples
  were solved with; Ubuntu 26.04 has 2.21. When Debian's calculix-ccx is
  2.23 or newer (or GridForge accepts the archive's version, saying which
  ccx solved each run as it already does), gridforge-calculix should
  depend on calculix-ccx and drop the ccx and spooles components.

Each is a change to debian/control and debian/rules only.
